a las vegas woman though has traveled  across the world to help the millions  who've escaped the war in ukraine and  she's helping families get back on their  feet in both poland and prague sasha  loftis joining us after speaking to that  woman and another woman who's trying to  get to the u.s  denise and brian these two women are  from opposite sides of the world one  from here in las vegas another from  ukraine they hope this story helps  others understand that those who've  escaped the war still need help  you cannot believe that it is happening  in  our time and in on our planet a month  after she was forced from her home in  ukraine victoria dichenko shares  everything she's been through we didn't  eat we didn't sleep we heard everything  all this bombardment she and her mom  left everything behind in keith  remembering what their home once was and  adjusting to life as refugees in krakow  poland we want to go somewhere else but  but what we can do they're among about 4  million who are now looking for a  permanent place to stay and las vegas  kathy healey has traveled there to  volunteer  everybody told me you need to go to  krakow to help and that's how the two  found each other victoria walked over to  my table  she was in the same restaurant with her  mother  and she said to me  can you help what victoria wants more  than anything else is to live and work  in the u.s  but she's hit some logistical roadblocks  so she and kathy hope someone out there  could have the right connections  everybody deserves a second chance so  this woman can forge her path  and start over  after a journey few could ever imagine  we don't know what and when will happen  this is limited in poland right now so  victoria has a friend in the u.s that's  paying for she and her mom to stay in a  hotel for the next four days but after  that they will once again be looking for  a place to stay
 

